# The trial of pod_hold::connect and pod_hold::packet in podnet (T-169, T-170
# step 1). connect.rs of podnet-netns becomes glue over pod_hold::connect:
# the state of the dials (Dials, ErrorCall, Caller, the join, the start, the
# finish, the taker, the answers and the write of an SO_ERROR) comes from the
# crate; podnet keeps Dialed, the channel of the ends of the dials, the dial,
# the rules, the entry of the socket, the hand-off and the relays.
# netns/packet.rs takes parse_tcp_syn, rst_reply_for_syn and ipv4_checksum
# from pod_hold::packet and keeps dns_reply_packet. The tests
# parses_a_tcp_syn, the_rst_reply_answers_the_syn,
# a_header_shorter_than_20_bytes_is_no_syn and
# a_fragment_past_the_first_is_no_syn of lib.rs move to pod-hold. Each
# podcrates tag moves to v0.17.0. The record, the size and the layers of the
# files, the build, the bans and the sources of cargo-deny, no copy of the
# moved items left in podnet, clippy of the workspace, the docs of
# podnet-netns, the tests of podnet-netns and of each crate whose podcrates
# tag moved, the integration tests of the pod (seccomp and netns: the waits
# of a nonblocking connect, a slow dial, the hand-off, the RST of a refused
# SYN), doctor, docs and the API, the fuzz targets with their lock, rustfmt,
# each Rust toolchain of the workflows and build images against the
# rust-version of podcrates, and the binary for x86_64 musl, built with zig
# (a debug build: the release profile takes LTO), with podnet's static check
# of it.
cargo run -q -p podnet-todo -- remap Cargo.lock > /dev/null
cargo run -q -p podnet-todo -- check
python3 scripts/check-size.py
python3 scripts/check-layers.py
cargo build -q
command -v cargo-deny > /dev/null || cargo install -q --locked cargo-deny
cargo deny --locked check bans sources
cargo tree -q -p podnet-netns -i pod-hold > /dev/null
! git grep -n -E "struct Waiting|struct ErrorCall|struct Caller|fn answer_error|fn parse_tcp_syn|fn rst_reply_for_syn|fn ipv4_checksum" -- crates src
cargo clippy -q --workspace --all-targets -- -D warnings
RUSTDOCFLAGS="-D warnings" cargo doc -q --no-deps -p podnet-netns
cargo test -q -p podnet-netns
cargo test -q -p podnet-core -p podnet-serve -p podnet-vnet --lib
cargo test -q -p podnet --test pod_seccomp --test pod_seccomp_tcp --test pod_seccomp_dgram --test pod_seccomp_fds --test pod_seccomp_handoff --test pod_seccomp_nonblock --test pod_seccomp_rules --test pod_seccomp_slow_dial --test pod_seccomp_diff --test pod_backend_line --test pod_usage --test af_inet_kernel --test doctor --test docs --test api_surface
cargo update -q -w --manifest-path fuzz/Cargo.toml
cargo check -q --manifest-path fuzz/Cargo.toml --bins
cargo fmt --all --check
python3 -I "$PODCRATES/scripts/check-consumer-toolchains.py"
cargo zigbuild -q --target x86_64-unknown-linux-musl -p podnet --bin podnet
sh scripts/check-static.sh "${CARGO_TARGET_DIR:-target}/x86_64-unknown-linux-musl/debug/podnet"
